title: "Drought Intelligence Explorer: a multi-era district drought record and analytics platform for India"
version: "2.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24444860
date-released: 2026-11-22
authors:
  - family-names: Deshmukh
    given-names: Ankit
    orcid: 0000-0002-1433-3872
    affiliation: "Pandit Deendayal Energy University"
    website: https://ankitdeshmukh.com/
repository-code: https://github.com/anixn/drought-intelligence-explorer
url: https://drought.ankitdeshmukh.com/
abstract: "A fully static, client-side geospatial platform and its reproducible Python pipelines for district-level drought analysis across India, spanning three explicitly labelled eras that are never spliced: the Drought Atlas of India SPEI reconstruction (1901-2025, served at district level), an observation-based gridded multi-source product (SPI-1/3/6/12, SPEI-1/3/6/12, soil-moisture anomaly and VCI, 1981-2026-09, from CHIRPS v2.0, ERA5-Land and MODIS MOD13A3), and bias-corrected CMIP6 projections (2015-2100, SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5, ensemble median, spread and model agreement) for 724 districts. Missing values are never imputed; every statistic reports its sample size; an independent IMD benchmark and an era A/era B cross-validation are published with the record."
